    "notes": "Interior species (Zoo 0.84.0). REFERENCE: a seven-foot coin-op bar table of the 1990s (Valley / Dynamo type): a heavy wood-grain cabinet on corner posts, rails with inlaid sights, black pocket castings at the corners and the middle of each long side, cushions with angled noses, bar-green / blue / burgundy cloth, a steel coin slide and a ball-return window on one end; a few balls where the game stopped and, on most seeds, a cue across the cloth. Geometry planned purely in core/pool_table_forms.py. BUILT (0.84.0): 1360 tris at 2.0 x 1.14 x 0.79, 1468 at 2.8 x 1.6 x 0.84 and 1.8 x 1.0 x 0.76 with a cue. Balls are 48 tris each (8 x 4 facets), sights 12. BUDGET 1600: one or two per bar, the hero of the room it is in."
